# CODEOWNERS — reviewed-lane ownership for the auto-merge lane.
# Owned paths require code-owner review; the trailing unowned block clears the
# auto-merge-lane paths so they need none. Last-match-wins, so the unowned block
# is LAST. Owned paths are reviewed; unowned (trailing) paths auto-merge.

# --- Reviewed lane: all code + constitutional docs (review required) -------
* @andrewRCr

# Constitutional surfaces, called out explicitly.
/.arc/system/rules/DEV-RULES.* @andrewRCr
/.arc/reference/adr/ @andrewRCr
/.arc/reference/strategies/ @andrewRCr

# --- Auto-merge lane: per-WU / per-cohort planning artifacts (UNOWNED) ------
# No owner clears the catch-all above. Scoped by artifact PREFIX, not all of
# backlog/ — so derived / shared surfaces (ROADMAP, the *-INBOX queues) keep the
# catch-all owner and stay reviewed. Specs and PRDs are absent by design.
/.arc/active/draft-*
/.arc/active/tasks-*
/.arc/active/meta-*
/.arc/active/notes-*
/.arc/backlog/**/draft-*
/.arc/backlog/**/tasks-*
/.arc/backlog/**/meta-*
/.arc/backlog/**/notes-*
/.arc/backlog/**/cohort-*
